<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ibrahim Pasha of Egypt</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1789">1789</a>–<a href="/years/1848">1848</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ibrahim Pasha of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> was the eldest son of Muhammad Ali and the chief commander of his armies. He destroyed the Saudi capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diriyah">Diriyah</a> in 1818, fought in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> in the 1820s, and conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> in 1831–1833, defeating the Ottoman army at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konya">Konya</a>. In 1848 he briefly ruled Egypt as regent for his ailing father.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ibrahim-pasha-of-egypt.jpg" alt="Ibrahim Pasha of Egypt" width="320" height="430" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charles-Philippe Larivière · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ibrahim_Pasha,_Larivi%C3%A8re.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
